  "hindi": "होता, जानता हुआ, दीप्तिमान्, चमकता हुआ, अत्यन्त कुशल, होता के आसन पर बैठ गया है; अहिंसित व्रत वाला और सावधान, सर्वश्रेष्ठ, हज़ारों का वहन करने वाला, उज्ज्वल जिह्वा वाला अग्नि।",
  "english": "The Hotṛ priest has sat down in the seat of the Hotṛ, knowing, blazing, shining, very skilful; Agni, of unharmed ordinance and careful, the most excellent, bearer of thousands, bright-tongued.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "adabdha-vrata-pramatiḥ: pramati is 'forethought, care'; the compound is taken as 'whose care is for unharmed ordinances' or 'of unharmed ordinance, careful'; the exact sense is not certain. vasiṣṭhaḥ is taken as the superlative of vasu, 'most excellent'; it may also be the name Vasiṣṭha. vidānaḥ: from √vid 'know' (alternatively 'finding'). sahasram-bharaḥ literally 'bearing a thousand'.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "type": "verse",
