  "hindi": "हे अग्नि, हम तुम्हारी सर्वोच्च उत्पत्ति में उपासना करें; हम निम्नतर सहस्थान में स्तोमों से उपासना करें। जिस योनि से तुम ऊपर उठे, उसकी मैं उपासना करता हूँ; प्रज्वलित तुममें हवियाँ अर्पित की जाती हैं।",
  "english": "May we worship you, O Agni, in the highest birth; may we worship with praises in the lower common seat. I worship that source from which you arose; in you, kindled, the oblations are offered.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "yoneḥ ud ārithāḥ: the printed token yonerudārithā is read as yoneḥ ud ārithāḥ; ārithāḥ is taken as a 2 sg. middle aorist of √ṛ with ud, 'you rose up'; the form is not certain. yaje taṃ: 'that' is taken as the source (yoni). juhure is a perfect with present sense 'are offered'. janmann: locative of janman. tam is masculine accusative and could also be Agni himself ('I worship him'); the translation takes it as the source (yoni).",
