  "hindi": "हे अग्नि, तुम हवि से यजन करो, श्रेष्ठ यजन करने वाले बनकर; शीघ्रता से दान को, उदारता को घोषित करो। क्योंकि तुम धनों के धनपति हो; तुम उज्ज्वल वाणी के विचारक हो।",
  "english": "O Agni, worship with the oblation, as the best worshipper; readily proclaim the gift, the bounty. For you are the lord of wealth of riches; you are the thinker of the bright speech.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "yajīyān śruṣṭī: yajīyān is the comparative 'better/best at worshipping'; śruṣṭī is taken as an adverb 'readily'; both are uncertain. deṣṇam abhi gṛṇīhi rādhaḥ: the construction (both nouns as objects of abhi gṛṇīhi) is tentative. rayipatī is the long-ī form of rayipatiḥ (Vedic lengthening); not treated as an error. manotā: agent noun 'thinker'.",
